1
00:00:14,520 --> 00:00:18,440
‎BEWARE FIRE
‎CIGARETTE BUTTS HERE

2
00:00:29,660 --> 00:00:31,040
‎KEEP CLOSED

3
00:00:31,040 --> 00:00:33,080
‎Yo, Sasaki.

4
00:00:33,710 --> 00:00:35,840
‎Hello.

5
00:00:36,880 --> 00:00:38,340
‎The hell, man?

6
00:00:38,340 --> 00:00:41,590
‎I couldn't find you in the smoking room
‎downstairs, so I had to come looking.

7
00:00:42,670 --> 00:00:44,590
‎Sorry.

8
00:00:44,590 --> 00:00:46,090
‎Is everything all right?

9
00:00:55,100 --> 00:00:57,310
‎The department manager
‎wants a meeting after this.

10
00:00:58,690 --> 00:00:59,980
‎For God's sake.

11
00:01:00,690 --> 00:01:05,610
‎Another pointless meeting that could
‎have been an email that will go on and on…

12
00:01:06,110 --> 00:01:07,570
‎All right, all right.

13
00:01:16,370 --> 00:01:18,710
‎I just wanna go home.

14
00:01:25,090 --> 00:01:26,340
‎Me too.

15
00:03:04,070 --> 00:03:07,490
‎HAPPY CORP.

16
00:03:19,710 --> 00:03:22,710
‎PUT SNACKS HERE

17
00:03:41,440 --> 00:03:42,900
‎LOCAL

18
00:04:34,280 --> 00:04:36,990
‎OPEN 24 HOURS - SUPER S

19
00:04:49,670 --> 00:04:50,670
‎SUPER S

20
00:04:56,550 --> 00:04:58,220
‎HALF PRICE - SQUID AND CHINESE RADISH

21
00:05:01,560 --> 00:05:04,980
‎ALCOHOL SECTION

22
00:05:15,200 --> 00:05:19,200
‎CRACKERS

23
00:05:20,580 --> 00:05:22,580
‎TASTY RICE CRACKERS

24
00:05:25,830 --> 00:05:27,500
‎Thank you, and have a nice day.

25
00:05:30,210 --> 00:05:31,500
‎Hello, and welcome!

26
00:05:34,260 --> 00:05:36,220
‎Do you have a point card?

27
00:05:36,220 --> 00:05:38,140
‎Yes, I do.

28
00:05:38,970 --> 00:05:40,010
‎Thank you.

29
00:05:42,060 --> 00:05:43,810
‎Here is your card back.

30
00:05:50,360 --> 00:05:52,530
‎Would you like a bag?

31
00:05:53,110 --> 00:05:54,900
‎Just the three-yen one, please.

32
00:05:54,900 --> 00:05:58,740
‎With the bag, your total comes to 883 yen.

33
00:05:58,740 --> 00:05:59,780
‎Here.

34
00:06:07,830 --> 00:06:09,920
‎Here is your change.

35
00:06:10,880 --> 00:06:12,010
‎Thank you.

36
00:06:14,760 --> 00:06:16,470
‎Thank you, and have a nice day.

37
00:06:21,510 --> 00:06:23,760
‎CASHIER: YAMADA

38
00:06:23,770 --> 00:06:26,060
‎Yamada from register two.

39
00:06:26,770 --> 00:06:29,560
‎My ray of light
‎at the end of a long work day.

40
00:06:32,150 --> 00:06:33,740
‎Then again…

41
00:06:34,530 --> 00:06:38,450
‎I'm dropping by way too much these days, 
‎even when I don't really need anything.

42
00:06:38,450 --> 00:06:40,700
‎What a stupid purchase I've made.

43
00:06:41,320 --> 00:06:44,320
‎I might as well bring a gift
‎for Yamada while I'm at it.

44
00:06:44,830 --> 00:06:46,460
‎She might actually like that.

45
00:06:46,450 --> 00:06:47,530
‎TASTY RICE CRACKERS

46
00:06:47,540 --> 00:06:50,000
‎Wow! Thank you so much!

47
00:06:53,960 --> 00:06:58,920
‎Guess it's delusional old men like me
‎who go around causing awkward situations.

48
00:07:00,430 --> 00:07:03,430
‎What the hell
‎is going on with you, Sasaki?

49
00:07:03,430 --> 00:07:07,680
‎Did you suddenly forget that doing client
‎rounds doesn't equate to a nice stroll?

50
00:07:07,680 --> 00:07:11,770
‎For God's sake, man.
‎You gotta let me know about these things!

51
00:07:11,770 --> 00:07:13,310
‎I'm very sorry, sir.

52
00:07:13,310 --> 00:07:17,060
‎Use your words, Sasaki!
‎Remember to use your words!

53
00:07:17,070 --> 00:07:19,200
‎People are gonna ask
‎if I'm fit to manage--

54
00:07:19,200 --> 00:07:21,620
‎Sir. Sorry to interrupt.

55
00:07:22,120 --> 00:07:26,000
‎Eda from Square Corp.
‎is asking about that quote.

56
00:07:26,700 --> 00:07:29,120
‎Tell him we'll respond sometime tomorrow.

57
00:07:30,250 --> 00:07:32,840
‎So terribly sorry to keep you waiting!

58
00:07:32,830 --> 00:07:35,790
‎Yes. It'll be ready tomorrow.
‎Yes. Yes. I am truly sorry…

59
00:07:35,800 --> 00:07:37,510
‎Meeting at seven!

60
00:07:43,090 --> 00:07:45,550
‎That idiot running the department…

61
00:07:46,140 --> 00:07:50,690
‎Not only did we run until midnight, 
‎but also, nothing even got resolved.

62
00:07:50,690 --> 00:07:52,690
‎I'm gonna kill--

63
00:07:52,690 --> 00:07:54,230
‎Nobody.

64
00:07:54,730 --> 00:07:56,440
‎It's times like these…

65
00:07:56,440 --> 00:07:57,730
‎Especially times like these…

66
00:07:58,990 --> 00:08:00,780
‎I need Yamada tonight!

67
00:08:02,280 --> 00:08:04,870
‎Here is your change, deary.

68
00:08:04,870 --> 00:08:05,950
‎GLOOM

69
00:08:05,950 --> 00:08:07,620
‎Thank you, and have a nice day.

70
00:08:08,370 --> 00:08:09,370
‎Thank you.

71
00:08:12,750 --> 00:08:16,290
‎Yamada must be on her break, 
‎or gone home for the day.

72
00:08:16,290 --> 00:08:18,880
‎Things are just not going my way today.

73
00:08:20,170 --> 00:08:23,220
‎Please, nicotine. Don't fail me today.

74
00:08:24,470 --> 00:08:26,470
‎Ew, look.

75
00:08:26,470 --> 00:08:29,470
‎-Disgusting.
‎-Let's go.

76
00:08:36,980 --> 00:08:40,360
‎Don't tell me there's no smoking area?

77
00:08:40,360 --> 00:08:42,030
‎You have got to be kidding me.

78
00:08:42,030 --> 00:08:45,160
‎Since when did us smokers
‎lose all our basic rights?

79
00:08:45,160 --> 00:08:46,250
‎Hey, pops.

80
00:08:47,490 --> 00:08:49,280
‎Over here.

81
00:08:55,000 --> 00:08:57,250
‎Come join me for a drag.

82
00:08:58,880 --> 00:09:00,760
‎Such an attractive--

83
00:09:00,760 --> 00:09:04,600
‎Wait, 
‎is this the backside of the supermarket?

84
00:09:07,800 --> 00:09:10,390
‎Won't you get in trouble
‎for letting an outsider smoke here?

85
00:09:12,230 --> 00:09:15,820
‎Who's gonna tell
‎if you're an outsider or not?

86
00:09:16,690 --> 00:09:19,820
‎Well, then… I guess I'll join you.

87
00:09:19,820 --> 00:09:21,240
‎Please do.

88
00:09:35,540 --> 00:09:39,960
‎Not sure what scene she's into, 
‎but she sure does look intense.

89
00:09:40,840 --> 00:09:43,840
‎Certainly doesn't
‎look like she works here.

90
00:09:47,010 --> 00:09:52,470
‎So, ma'am. Which section
‎of the supermarket do you work--

91
00:09:55,850 --> 00:09:58,270
‎Come on. Gimme a light.

92
00:09:58,270 --> 00:09:59,980
‎Why else do you think I called you over?

93
00:10:00,690 --> 00:10:02,570
‎Then you should have just said so!

94
00:10:02,570 --> 00:10:04,860
‎I felt like joshing with you.

95
00:10:06,200 --> 00:10:08,620
‎You shouldn't "josh"
‎someone you've only just met.

96
00:10:16,330 --> 00:10:20,460
‎You're the guy who's always
‎lining up at register two, ain't ya?

97
00:10:23,800 --> 00:10:26,220
‎Am I? Must be coincidence.

98
00:10:27,260 --> 00:10:30,930
‎Is it also a coincidence that you line up
‎even when other registers are open?

99
00:10:30,930 --> 00:10:32,600
‎She knows my whole routine.

100
00:10:33,470 --> 00:10:35,600
‎You like Little Miss Yamada, don't you?

101
00:10:37,100 --> 00:10:39,900
‎She already knows the answer, 
‎and still she chooses to tease me?

102
00:10:41,020 --> 00:10:42,730
‎I get it.

103
00:10:42,730 --> 00:10:44,650
‎She's a sweet girl, that Yamada.

104
00:10:45,860 --> 00:10:48,780
‎Nice on the eyes, and a nice rack to boot.

105
00:10:48,780 --> 00:10:51,490
‎And she's single, 
‎which must delight you, no?

106
00:10:51,490 --> 00:10:52,950
‎That's not true!

107
00:10:52,950 --> 00:10:57,700
‎Yes, I know I'm just some creepy guy
‎who likes to line up at Yamada's register.

108
00:10:57,710 --> 00:11:01,760
‎But honestly, it's just that her
‎work ethic is what keeps me going!

109
00:11:02,420 --> 00:11:04,670
‎That's all I'm allowed
‎to be "delighted" about!

110
00:11:09,130 --> 00:11:10,590
‎Sorry.

111
00:11:10,590 --> 00:11:12,470
‎I got a bit carried away there.

112
00:11:14,180 --> 00:11:16,020
‎-Well, that's a relief.
‎-Huh?

113
00:11:16,600 --> 00:11:20,100
‎I thought Yamada
‎had herself another shitty customer.

114
00:11:20,100 --> 00:11:24,020
‎She gets a lot of idiots
‎pestering her about that sort of thing.

115
00:11:26,110 --> 00:11:28,780
‎But you're not like that.

116
00:11:31,320 --> 00:11:35,200
‎Work hard, and stay sophisticated, Sasaki.

117
00:11:39,040 --> 00:11:42,580
‎I thought she was just an ill-mannered
‎young lady who picks on older men, 

118
00:11:42,580 --> 00:11:45,290
‎but it would seem she's a good kid
‎who looks out for her coworkers.

119
00:11:46,170 --> 00:11:47,260
‎Um…

120
00:11:48,920 --> 00:11:51,340
‎Excuse me, but you need to pay.

121
00:11:51,340 --> 00:11:53,340
‎Sorry.

122
00:12:00,020 --> 00:12:01,690
‎Mr. Sasaki?

123
00:12:01,690 --> 00:12:04,690
‎Huh? How do you know my name?

124
00:12:04,690 --> 00:12:08,530
‎I've known your name for a while now
‎because of your point card.

125
00:12:10,530 --> 00:12:11,990
‎I wanted to thank you.

126
00:12:13,570 --> 00:12:16,160
‎I've been speaking with Tayama.

127
00:12:16,160 --> 00:12:18,620
‎-I'm very happy to hear it.
‎-Huh?

128
00:12:18,620 --> 00:12:21,370
‎She says you're a fan of mine.

129
00:12:23,370 --> 00:12:24,620
‎You dropped your card.

130
00:12:25,290 --> 00:12:26,750
‎Sorry about that.

131
00:12:29,090 --> 00:12:30,840
‎Thank you, and have a nice day.

132
00:12:30,840 --> 00:12:34,140
‎Goddamn it, Tayama.

133
00:12:35,010 --> 00:12:37,010
‎Don't think I won't remember that name!

134
00:12:37,680 --> 00:12:39,600
‎Yo. I'm Tayama.

135
00:12:46,310 --> 00:12:50,020
‎See you at the smoking area, Sasaki.

136
00:12:50,650 --> 00:12:54,610
‎Actually, how did Tayama know my name?

137
00:13:05,000 --> 00:13:07,750
‎HAPPY CORP.

138
00:13:07,750 --> 00:13:11,210
‎Another meeting
‎till midnight tonight, huh?

139
00:13:11,210 --> 00:13:15,420
‎I hope someone goes apeshit
‎and trashes the meeting for us.

140
00:13:16,340 --> 00:13:18,510
‎Meeting this, meeting that.
‎About what, even?

141
00:13:18,510 --> 00:13:20,390
‎SMOKING ROOM

142
00:13:20,390 --> 00:13:23,440
‎Everyone's on edge
‎from all these back-to-back meetings.

143
00:13:25,770 --> 00:13:27,980
‎Even me…

144
00:13:28,480 --> 00:13:31,690
‎But I've got the best pick-me-up!

145
00:13:32,190 --> 00:13:35,320
‎The smile of Yamada
‎from Super S register two!

146
00:13:35,320 --> 00:13:37,660
‎Hello, and welcome!
‎Thank you, and have a nice day.

147
00:13:37,660 --> 00:13:41,290
‎You're the guy who's always
‎lining up at register two, ain't ya?

148
00:14:17,740 --> 00:14:19,490
‎She's not here.

149
00:14:25,160 --> 00:14:26,740
‎Thank you, and have a nice day.

150
00:14:26,750 --> 00:14:29,300
‎Oh, what brilliant timing!

151
00:14:30,380 --> 00:14:33,970
‎She says you're a fan of mine.

152
00:14:36,420 --> 00:14:37,670
‎Next, please.

153
00:14:40,140 --> 00:14:41,600
‎Hello, and welcome!

154
00:14:42,310 --> 00:14:43,980
‎Just these, please.

155
00:14:44,470 --> 00:14:47,310
‎All right. Do you have a point card?

156
00:14:48,730 --> 00:14:51,110
‎-I do.
‎-Thank you.

157
00:14:52,610 --> 00:14:54,280
‎Here's your card back.

158
00:14:56,570 --> 00:14:58,610
‎I've been speaking with Tayama.

159
00:14:58,610 --> 00:15:00,240
‎She says you're a fan of mine.

160
00:15:03,580 --> 00:15:05,540
‎Sir? Sir?

161
00:15:05,540 --> 00:15:06,750
‎Yes?

162
00:15:06,750 --> 00:15:09,080
‎That'll be 883 yen.

163
00:15:09,080 --> 00:15:11,080
‎Sorry.

164
00:15:14,800 --> 00:15:18,800
‎I exposed myself
‎as a gross and bumbling idiot, 

165
00:15:18,800 --> 00:15:21,300
‎but I'm glad she still chose
‎to serve me politely.

166
00:15:22,390 --> 00:15:24,430
‎I'm the only one getting weird about this!

167
00:15:24,430 --> 00:15:25,720
‎Moron! Idiot!

168
00:15:26,930 --> 00:15:30,390
‎From now on, I'm going to just
‎quietly get on with my shopping.

169
00:15:31,190 --> 00:15:33,480
‎Do as you see fit.

170
00:15:43,820 --> 00:15:47,620
‎That client still hasn't gotten
‎back to me after I sent that apology.

171
00:15:47,620 --> 00:15:50,830
‎I'm gonna die
‎without ever seeing my family again.

172
00:15:50,830 --> 00:15:51,910
‎KEEP THINGS TIDY AND IN ORDER

173
00:15:51,920 --> 00:15:53,250
‎Next to this old geezer.

174
00:15:53,250 --> 00:15:55,130
‎Would you give it a rest already?

175
00:15:55,130 --> 00:15:57,470
‎And why are you here
‎doing overtime anyway?

176
00:15:57,960 --> 00:16:01,130
‎I'm fixing up those files the newbie did.

177
00:16:01,130 --> 00:16:03,220
‎Are you letting them walk all over you?

178
00:16:03,220 --> 00:16:06,850
‎No, they really shouldn't have given this
‎sort of work to a newbie to begin with.

179
00:16:06,850 --> 00:16:08,600
‎That department manager, am I right?

180
00:16:08,600 --> 00:16:12,230
‎"Throw 'em in the deep end.
‎That's the best way to learn."

181
00:16:12,230 --> 00:16:15,320
‎Then he leaves the mess
‎they make to everyone else.

182
00:16:17,530 --> 00:16:21,160
‎Well, either way, 
‎the poor newbie's got it the hardest.

183
00:16:21,150 --> 00:16:25,240
‎I can tell by these files
‎that a lot of heart went into this.

184
00:16:26,240 --> 00:16:28,580
‎And besides… I've got my pick-me-up.

185
00:16:29,200 --> 00:16:30,780
‎Hello, and welcome!

186
00:16:30,790 --> 00:16:32,960
‎This is nothing when I know I've got--

187
00:16:32,960 --> 00:16:36,300
‎Oh? It's Mr. Fan.

188
00:16:42,300 --> 00:16:44,760
‎I just deleted all my updates!

189
00:16:46,350 --> 00:16:48,690
‎This calls for a celebration!

190
00:16:50,770 --> 00:16:53,020
‎Thank you, and have a nice day.

191
00:16:53,020 --> 00:16:54,230
‎Thanks. You too.

192
00:16:55,020 --> 00:16:56,560
‎She wasn't there.

193
00:16:57,060 --> 00:16:58,770
‎It's like the universe is saying, 

194
00:16:58,770 --> 00:17:01,770
‎"Serves you right, Sasaki, 
‎for seeking solace through others."

195
00:17:02,780 --> 00:17:05,369
‎I really need to find
‎a hobby or something.

196
00:17:05,869 --> 00:17:07,079
‎Sasaki.

197
00:17:08,579 --> 00:17:09,790
‎'Sup?

198
00:17:12,040 --> 00:17:15,210
‎The smoking spot's empty, you know?

199
00:17:15,210 --> 00:17:16,300
‎Wanna join me?

200
00:17:21,260 --> 00:17:25,510
‎Tayama! I… have a bone to pick with you.

201
00:17:26,180 --> 00:17:28,060
‎How could you?

202
00:17:28,050 --> 00:17:30,510
‎You told Yamada I was a fan of hers.

203
00:17:30,510 --> 00:17:33,550
‎Now I'm too embarrassed
‎to line up at her register.

204
00:17:33,560 --> 00:17:35,690
‎But you still line up for her.

205
00:17:36,900 --> 00:17:38,610
‎How did you see that?

206
00:17:45,030 --> 00:17:47,620
‎Sorry for being a meanie, Sasaki.

207
00:17:50,490 --> 00:17:52,830
‎But Yamada was very happy to hear it.

208
00:17:53,330 --> 00:17:55,710
‎She said it herself, right?

209
00:17:55,710 --> 00:18:00,170
‎I'm not some kid who takes
‎everything at face value. You know?

210
00:18:01,500 --> 00:18:03,670
‎Is that the only bone you had to pick?

211
00:18:04,340 --> 00:18:05,630
‎And…

212
00:18:06,220 --> 00:18:08,470
‎Here. These are for you.

213
00:18:08,470 --> 00:18:09,550
‎TASTY RICE CRACKERS

214
00:18:09,550 --> 00:18:12,970
‎As thanks for letting me
‎smoke with you the other day.

215
00:18:12,970 --> 00:18:14,300
‎Hey, nice!

216
00:18:14,310 --> 00:18:17,230
‎You know them? "Tasty Rice Crackers."

217
00:18:17,230 --> 00:18:18,980
‎I love them.

218
00:18:18,980 --> 00:18:22,480
‎These are really popular
‎with the old folks, huh?

219
00:18:23,570 --> 00:18:25,490
‎Am I really that old to her?

220
00:18:26,490 --> 00:18:28,410
‎I've been meaning to try these.

221
00:18:28,910 --> 00:18:30,910
‎Thanks, Sasaki.

222
00:18:30,910 --> 00:18:33,500
‎Well, don't just stand there.
‎Come smoke next to me.

223
00:18:33,490 --> 00:18:37,370
‎Oh? She likes her gift
‎from an elderly fellow?

224
00:18:37,870 --> 00:18:40,670
‎Tayama. Do you like things
‎that have come full circle?

225
00:18:41,290 --> 00:18:44,210
‎I'm a little hungry after my shift.

226
00:18:44,710 --> 00:18:47,000
‎Well, don't eat them all.

227
00:18:47,010 --> 00:18:49,100
‎Wouldn't want to strain
‎yourself before bed--

228
00:18:53,390 --> 00:18:55,930
‎I left my smokes back at work.

229
00:18:56,730 --> 00:18:58,270
‎I'm flat out.

230
00:18:59,600 --> 00:19:01,310
‎Here. You can have mine.

231
00:19:01,900 --> 00:19:03,820
‎No, I couldn't ask that of you.

232
00:19:05,190 --> 00:19:06,320
‎Take it.

233
00:19:08,820 --> 00:19:10,070
‎Tayama?

234
00:19:12,160 --> 00:19:15,250
‎If it's in the way of your crackers, 
‎just say so.

235
00:19:15,240 --> 00:19:18,120
‎Wow, Sasaki. Very perceptive.

236
00:19:19,960 --> 00:19:23,340
‎Do you enjoy teasing old men, Tayama?

237
00:19:23,340 --> 00:19:24,800
‎Very much so.

238
00:19:24,800 --> 00:19:26,220
‎I'll bet it's fun!

239
00:19:26,800 --> 00:19:28,510
‎Can you blame me?

240
00:19:28,510 --> 00:19:31,140
‎You're like my stress relief.

241
00:19:31,140 --> 00:19:33,430
‎What? Stress relief?

242
00:19:33,430 --> 00:19:36,640
‎Just like how you
‎line up for Yamada's register.

243
00:19:37,520 --> 00:19:39,730
‎Now you're teasing me again.

244
00:19:40,230 --> 00:19:44,480
‎Unlike you, I don't pick on Yamada.

245
00:19:44,480 --> 00:19:46,690
‎You don't get it, do you?

246
00:19:47,190 --> 00:19:49,570
‎We all have our different
‎ways of relieving stress.

247
00:19:50,070 --> 00:19:51,910
‎So please don't pout.

248
00:19:52,410 --> 00:19:54,830
‎I hope I'll see you again, Sasaki.

249
00:19:57,910 --> 00:20:00,450
‎I'm not pouting.

250
00:20:05,420 --> 00:20:07,300
‎Morning.

251
00:20:07,300 --> 00:20:09,050
‎PUT SNACKS HERE

252
00:20:09,050 --> 00:20:11,760
‎TASTY RICE CRACKERS

253
00:20:13,300 --> 00:20:16,090
‎How was the client?

254
00:20:16,100 --> 00:20:21,440
‎Oh, yeah. I'm a master apologizer, 
‎so we got it all worked out.

255
00:20:24,190 --> 00:20:26,110
‎Are these rice crackers yours?

256
00:20:26,690 --> 00:20:27,980
‎How did you know?

257
00:20:27,980 --> 00:20:29,230
‎Are you brain-dead?

258
00:20:29,240 --> 00:20:31,530
‎Do you even know how many times
‎you've made me eat these?

259
00:20:32,700 --> 00:20:36,120
‎Once you start, 
‎you can't just stop at one with these.

260
00:20:36,120 --> 00:20:38,910
‎They go well with alcohol.
‎You should take them home with you.

261
00:20:38,910 --> 00:20:41,370
‎I will! I'll be taking the whole bag!

262
00:20:42,330 --> 00:20:44,870
‎But why do you have so many?

263
00:20:45,710 --> 00:20:48,050
‎Did you buy in bulk, or something?

264
00:20:48,550 --> 00:20:50,840
‎I kind of just got them
‎when I went to the supermarket.

265
00:20:51,340 --> 00:20:54,010
‎I forgot I already bought some, 
‎so now I have extra.

266
00:20:54,590 --> 00:20:56,800
‎What? Then just stop buying them.

267
00:20:57,300 --> 00:21:00,590
‎But then I won't have a reason
‎to go to the supermarket.

268
00:21:00,600 --> 00:21:02,850
‎Then stop going to the supermarket!

269
00:21:03,350 --> 00:21:05,850
‎OPEN 24 HOURS - SUPER S

270
00:21:05,850 --> 00:21:11,150
‎CRACKERS

271
00:21:13,280 --> 00:21:15,620
‎Just stop buying them, okay?

272
00:21:22,370 --> 00:21:23,790
‎Hello, and welcome!

273
00:21:27,210 --> 00:21:30,130
‎You're always getting these.
‎They're delicious, right?

274
00:21:30,130 --> 00:21:31,210
‎Huh?

275
00:21:31,210 --> 00:21:33,880
‎You like them too?

276
00:21:33,880 --> 00:21:35,090
‎I do.

277
00:21:35,090 --> 00:21:37,380
‎But only just recently.

278
00:21:37,890 --> 00:21:41,270
‎Somebody gave me some to try, 
‎and I found they were so delicious.

279
00:21:41,270 --> 00:21:43,020
‎I couldn't stop at just one.

280
00:21:43,020 --> 00:21:45,560
‎Somebody gave her some?

281
00:21:45,560 --> 00:21:47,440
‎They're good rice crackers.

282
00:21:48,020 --> 00:21:51,060
‎Could it be… Could it be?

283
00:21:51,570 --> 00:21:53,950
‎Could Yamada and Tayama be…

284
00:21:56,530 --> 00:21:59,030
‎They must be really good friends.

285
00:22:00,080 --> 00:22:01,250
‎Try these.

286
00:22:01,240 --> 00:22:03,080
‎Wow. Thank you!

287
00:22:04,790 --> 00:22:06,880
‎Yamada. Do you have allergies?

288
00:22:07,620 --> 00:22:08,870
‎No.

289
00:22:08,880 --> 00:22:13,260
‎It's probably just some dense old guy
‎getting delusional about me.

290
00:23:45,970 --> 00:23:50,980
‎Subtitle translation by: Rychelle Brittain
